commit 6552c0d5994c01a737dcd54c432dce87ddd9098d
Author: Volker Krause <vkrause@kde.org>
Date:   Sun Nov 15 14:00:35 2026 +0100

    android: Don't add Material style into the style chain unconditionally
    
    This didn't hurt so far, but since 6.32 we have Material-specific controls
    implementations here that are not in the Breeze style. This then makes
    applications only packaging the Breeze style fail to start now.
    
    Other cases should not be affected by this:
    * If Material is explicitly requested, style is already Material.
    * If there's not explicit style requested, Qt gives us Material as the
      default fallback.

diff --git a/src/platform/styleselector.cpp b/src/platform/styleselector.cpp
index 3938cfca8..13b5440e7 100644
--- a/src/platform/styleselector.cpp
+++ b/src/platform/styleselector.cpp
@@ -46,8 +46,6 @@ QStringList StyleSelector::styleChain()
 #if !defined(Q_OS_ANDROID) && !defined(Q_OS_IOS)
         u"org.kde.desktop.plasma"_s,
         u"org.kde.desktop"_s,
-#else
-        u"Material"_s,
 #endif
     };
 
